Using the gdb4hpc Comparative Debugging Feature demo sources

Certain components, files or programs contained within this package or product 
are Copyright 2013-2023 Hewlett Packard Enterprise Development LP.

To run the demos, do the following:

1. Ensure that the directory is currently placed within a cross mounted location
   such as a lustre file system.

2. Run the provided build_demo.sh build script. This will ensure a properly
   setup environment and automatically build all the necessary binaries.

3. Load the gdb4hpc module and start gdb4hpc. Start gdb4hpc with the --echo command so
   that commands from the provided .rc files are printed as they are executed.

4. Use the provided .rc files in the hpcc_scripts directory. The script can be used inside
   gdb4hpc using the source command. For example, if gdb4hpc is started from the parent
   directory, you would issue the following command:

      source hpcc_scripts/hpcc_script_1.rc

   Each .rc should be run from a new instance of gdb4hpc. An easy way to start a new
   gdb4hpc instance and immediately run an .rc file is:

      gdb4hpc --echo --exec "source hpcc_scripts/hpcc_script_1.rc"

   Or the equivalent shorter version:

      gdb4hpc -ex "source hpcc_scripts/hpcc_script_1.rc"

